`exponent` on a rational now uses only integer arithmetic, so values that `Float64` rounds onto a power of two keep the right exponent.

`exponent((2^60 - 1) // 2^60)` is `-1`. The result is `floor(log2(abs(numerator/denominator)))`: `exponent(numerator) - exponent(denominator)`, minus one when the absolute numerator is still below the denominator times that power of two. `|p| < |q|` alone is the wrong adjustment (`5//3` would become `1` instead of `0`).

